course: dictionary
lesson: 7292
title: Piranha: fact or film?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A dictionary tells you what a word means, but writers can use a word in a special way. Read the words around piranha to check which meaning the writer means, and whether they are talking about a fish or a person.
explain: «Films show piranhas stripping a cow in seconds» describes what films show. The sentence then gives the truth: «shy piranhas». Writers often put a myth next to a fact so the reader can compare them.
explain: Piranha can also describe a person. The dictionary marks this meaning as informal, which means relaxed everyday language. Look for clues like fierce, greedy, or attacking to know which meaning fits.
fact: A piranha is a South American river fish with very sharp, triangle-shaped teeth.
fact: Piranhas eat fish, insects, seeds and dead animals, and they are eaten by river dolphins, caimans and birds.
fact: Piranhas often swim in groups, mainly for safety.
fact: Films and cartoons make piranhas look like man-eaters, but real attacks on people are rare and usually just a bite.
fact: Informal: a piranha can also mean a fierce, greedy person who attacks others to get what they want.
exercise: «Cartoon piranhas turn a cow into a skeleton in seconds.» What does this sentence suggest about cartoons? | They show piranhas eating only plants | They never show animals | They are always accurate | *They make piranhas seem more dangerous than they really are
exercise: «Red-bellied piranhas have razor-sharp triangular teeth.» Which word tells you the shape of the teeth? | *triangular | red-bellied | razor-sharp | teeth
exercise: «When hunters killed most black caimans, piranhas grew in number, because caimans had been eating them.» Why did the piranhas grow in number? | *Fewer caimans were there to eat them | Hunters were feeding them | They learned to fly | They moved to the sea
test: Ella is a piranha in every board game, grabbing all the counters. What does piranha mean here? | A loud noise | *A fierce, greedy person | A type of boat | A river fish
test: Why do piranhas swim in groups? | To find the sea | Because they are lazy | *For safety | To look bigger
exam: Which food do piranhas eat? | Rocks | Only plants | Only cows | *Fish, insects, seeds and dead animals
